 disjoint" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={{2}^{n}∣n\\in N} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,16,…}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={2n∣n\\in N} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cap B & ={2,4,6,8,…}\\text{ }\\cap {2,4,8,16,…} \\\\  & ={2,4,8,…} \\\\  & \\ne ∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the intersection is not empty, the two sets are not disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa42f9bc-e3ad-56fa-8d82-4882e95ef826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Disjoint Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7bb5f41-fcb4-5d02-91d0-f31e1c3de7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453562} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f4a44e-d637-52cf-a887-73cc0d97a0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7bb5f41-fcb4-5d02-91d0-f31e1c3de7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453562} :answer-field/id #uuid "82819be0-362b-5e32-8302-b555769ba578" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91ac693-676b-513c-a120-28f5d225454e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453564} {:answer/id #uuid "649c0007-0213-5041-9308-8700b6b87c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "649c0007-0213-5041-9308-8700b6b87c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453565} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb77fee-c9a6-5eca-8070-75becb9ea8d3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a578522-5878-5e03-992a-88e669377c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453566} {:answer/id #uuid "29889270-0755-5b50-8a0b-f8d42377602d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29889270-0755-5b50-8a0b-f8d42377602d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453567} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8747fa0-0f7e-5d7b-b9ae-552b04cea01e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f863cc29-74d9-5551-a15b-2146bb98a0f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-174372" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{5n∣n\\in Z\\},\\,B=\\{-\\frac{1}{n}∣n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B=\\{-1,-2,-3,…\\}$\n\n- **II.** $A\\cap B=∅$\n\n- **III.** $A$ and $B$ are disjoint" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{-\\frac{1}{n}∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{3},…\\} \\\\  & \\ne \\{-1,-2,-3,…\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{5n∣n\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-10,-5,0,5,10,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\\{…,-10,-5,0,5,10,…\\}\\cap \\{-1,-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{3},…\\}=∅.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc424180-275c-5104-bb2f-801f5352d1e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453126} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6d9104-58b7-5756-8815-74bce3daeb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d6d9104-58b7-5756-8815-74bce3daeb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453127} :answer-field/id #uuid "d902d79e-6763-5342-80d1-d7399a1c3071" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3702e8-e0f2-57bc-9d4f-d249760952cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453128} {:answer/id #uuid "e7663072-82a6-5b49-84f6-83606c461d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7663072-82a6-5b49-84f6-83606c461d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453129} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f1d6375-82eb-5cfb-b555-3cde6d832a5c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cb3e985-0863-55c9-b7f5-f44b0aecc466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453130} {:answer/id #uuid "c069d807-3336-555f-a750-b47e4c202d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c069d807-3336-555f-a750-b47e4c202d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453131} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e0d476e-76f4-573b-aa99-5c5f27871d56" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0b7a4cb-746e-55f4-a074-7c8a26769a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103482" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $-5>-2,$ **then** $-2<-1.$\n- **II.** **If** $-5<-2,$ **then** $-2<-1.$\n- **III.** **If** $-5>-2,$ **then** $-2>-1.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent $-5>-2$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent $-5<-2$ is true, and the consequent $-2<-1$ is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $-5>-2$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "24b9af85-3717-59e0-aa72-d701f3c6b6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Nonlinear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e60d574e-9743-5291-b1e2-47b57717f06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453180} {:answer/id #uuid "742b291f-0b60-5b8a-9feb-5fbc63ebf086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e60d574e-9743-5291-b1e2-47b57717f06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453180} :answer-field/id #uuid "887d1f6a-2497-5159-b92c-e835954aff98" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07482126-2100-51de-b92e-48ba48007447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453182} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e0f9d8-f492-57c9-a192-36d5e6263f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2e0f9d8-f492-57c9-a192-36d5e6263f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453183} :answer-field/id #uuid "36c5ecf6-9b6c-56c5-9a7f-dc26b7b28cc9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f37e6a84-ed13-5bec-81d9-1c396370befe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453184} {:answer/id #uuid "ee74bce0-083a-5030-87f1-600504229e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee74bce0-083a-5030-87f1-600504229e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453185} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa7b08b-1be4-5762-b036-c96420944415" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5661c06a-c66c-5923-befb-278bbbf8f25e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105331" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36},\\,∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $P(0,-3)$ belongs to $A$\n- **II.** The point $P(0,-3)$ is a boundary point of $A$\n- **III.** The point $Q(0,2)$ is an interior point of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie inside the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/f3/f3b1df5f948603edcc1095da9215145cba21c7aebbdfdd6ab5cacecb5810efc7.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(0,-3)$ and $Q(0,2)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/7b/7bc1b41e3ca8aba5c1a5658ec421f7358041c57dea7c1ef45fe265c62664f097.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The coordinates of $P(0,-3)$ do not satisfy the inequality $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36.$ Hence, $P$ does not lie in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The coordinates of $P(0,-3)$ satisfy the equation $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $∂A,$ the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $Q$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $Q$ that is fully contained inside the set $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II and III only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "24b9af85-3717-59e0-aa72-d701f3c6b6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Nonlinear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa6a3646-f0f3-518d-83e8-d652aac9631a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453186} {:answer/id #uuid "abc7b05c-d177-5bd3-b0c0-c7d473c392d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abc7b05c-d177-5bd3-b0c0-c7d473c392d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453187} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad4d9fe-863c-51fe-b819-b9cd839172fa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e3ec6a-8bf8-591c-8390-ac4ee902b844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453188} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c76f95-7d8e-507d-bba0-2592577506ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10e3ec6a-8bf8-591c-8390-ac4ee902b844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453188} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c0619b-af68-5f6a-909b-32abdbd64822" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db96c2a1-daaa-5554-9596-3e9933aa3a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453190} {:answer/id #uuid "bddaa16e-05fb-57e6-8b2a-64267d599ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db96c2a1-daaa-5554-9596-3e9933aa3a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453190} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded76903-a98d-53d0-9797-9231cdcdfee6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab42b0ba-ecca-5e90-984d-305864760335" :question/math-academy-id "q-105336" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}\\ge 36},\\,∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $P(3,2)$ belongs to $A$\n- **II.** The point $P(3,2)$ is a boundary point of $A$\n- **III.** The point $Q(3,0)$ is an interior point of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie on or outside the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/67/67d1f23f424561c69973fe5f08ad3ee3a03346f555db8f00fb71406c02a9cdf9.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(3,2)$ and $Q(3,0)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/0b/0b3e72b3a65241c4e03716a9c0b534d687c305a92ceef0b92d5c6df8c1b82953.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of $P(3,2)$ satisfy the inequality $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}\\ge 36.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The coordinates of $P(3,2)$ do not satisfy the equation $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36.$ Hence, $P$ does not lie on the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Every open neighborhood of $Q$ contains points that belong to $A$ and points that do not belong to $A.$ The point $Q$ is a boundary point for the given set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce3c5f0-7529-5c2c-9564-44c889eb86c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453386} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0a7954-cd05-51a7-90b9-b780bf965f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce3c5f0-7529-5c2c-9564-44c889eb86c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453386} :answer-field/id #uuid "bca78a15-c48c-5741-abab-0bf7b97a57a4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454443} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcec78e2-d6bb-56c4-ad75-975ad764b8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453388} {:answer/id #uuid "292a5262-ac7c-5df9-a70a-6d1d92a3b30d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcec78e2-d6bb-56c4-ad75-975ad764b8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd94f480-acd9-57b8-a0ef-b55824c69c2f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dd8e82d-abc1-543c-9e38-eb7d06e6eeb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453390} {:answer/id #uuid "399ad536-9e21-50bb-b29b-6a5685869bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "399ad536-9e21-50bb-b29b-6a5685869bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453391} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcdeb836-29c1-560f-b756-552781011c7f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8048be79-9af8-51c0-a0c1-5b68f549139c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139986" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $3$\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since the generating vectors in \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nare linearly independent, we conclude that the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=1\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4.$ Now, according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9290da55-a6a3-5bb8-a9b8-2039b243ee6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453404} {:answer/id #uuid "adeaa133-0730-51b1-8b37-ab1eabd66c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adeaa133-0730-51b1-8b37-ab1eabd66c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453405} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f82a48-c4e0-5658-a295-60736c7e5166" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d7d24f-3606-50eb-9098-a34319240958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453406} {:answer/id #uuid "535a174d-2f6e-5ab0-99bb-3ccad768cc35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d7d24f-3606-50eb-9098-a34319240958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453406} :answer-field/id #uuid "59aa5f02-f270-5643-aeca-3ee7824a7629" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99558d31-6961-52e7-b662-299510c283b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453408} {:answer/id #uuid "688a37cc-bcaf-529c-a80d-90d43dc9aa3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99558d31-6961-52e7-b662-299510c283b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453408} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f387ba8-880e-5912-8b03-6a51150d10c2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "017db163-2592-561e-a975-d762dc265a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-142542" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}$\n- **III.** $A$ is  invertible" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=5,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=2\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 5$, according to the  invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64ba57cc-a3eb-582a-963b-b94895a20bac" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9d5b57d-d397-5e8b-9a46-ca703dc128d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453430} {:answer/id #uuid "654fdd13-26b0-5b13-a201-e47a6bbd127f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654fdd13-26b0-5b13-a201-e47a6bbd127f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453431} :answer-field/id #uuid "f245c56b-ea24-5bc6-9714-193572353072" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c17641c7-2616-5f44-913a-204e61d02795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453432} {:answer/id #uuid "1798276f-6c7e-5444-91e4-9f13f58ce650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1798276f-6c7e-5444-91e4-9f13f58ce650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453433} :answer-field/id #uuid "2595354c-4c90-5eb8-bc56-8aa27847f7cd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f28fa17-78af-5e9c-9940-0619d6581c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453434} {:answer/id #uuid "03c6eb37-ee8b-5456-b1b0-d792a68992e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f28fa17-78af-5e9c-9940-0619d6581c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453434} :answer-field/id #uuid "55044069-05bd-53df-bf38-5763c4c860a7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80400990-b978-5e6c-95c6-54cde07862e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-158534" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:y\\le x+2},\\,∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:y=x+2}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $P(2,4)$ lies on the boundary of $A$\n- **II.** The point $P(2,4)$ belongs to $A$\n- **III.** The point $Q(-2,3)$ is an interior point of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie on or below the line $y=x+2.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/3b/3b0505f0c1fb295665dd64c9d0f26f23960b638ef0e1d414c7ad306a89154dfb.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(2,4)$ and $Q(-2,3)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/62/623f00c423c7a846c52537d58c071c730083ba963fb488dbedbb76637ea9cc8c.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of $P(2,4)$ satisfy the equation $y=x+2.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $∂A,$ the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The coordinates of $P(2,4)$ satisfy the inequality $y\\le x+4.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, $Q$ is not an interior point of $A$ since any neighborhood of $Q$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and II only.'"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64ba57cc-a3eb-582a-963b-b94895a20bac" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points From Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2a38983-2ac2-5747-84de-52654204b669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453442} {:answer/id #uuid "24fa1281-9195-576c-958f-f5a1cd7756b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24fa1281-9195-576c-958f-f5a1cd7756b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453443} :answer-field/id #uuid "b974481d-3120-5f01-a603-07099f42a784" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454471} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f4a6e95-fed8-5f60-b3be-40a55090ad74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453444} {:answer/id #uuid "0fc66c24-39c8-55f8-949a-fd3c22a45e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f4a6e95-fed8-5f60-b3be-40a55090ad74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453444} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ab5754e-a652-5899-87ab-53e612a79fd5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c545dbcc-3d3d-5d7f-8c9e-39f107e5337c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453446} {:answer/id #uuid "7b177e0f-f566-534e-911c-092b634ea208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c545dbcc-3d3d-5d7f-8c9e-39f107e5337c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453446} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac4f957-7cd7-55eb-a39f-2fc8342eb8a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7257b8a6-8ea5-5027-98d4-5845f1b59c79" :question/math-academy-id "q-158548" :question/problem "The set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are given by\n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:y<x+3},\\,∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:y=x+3}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $P(-2,1)$ lies on the boundary of $A$\n- **II.** The point $P(-2,1)$ belongs to $A$\n- **III.** The point $Q(-2,3)$ is an interior point of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie below the line $y=x+3.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](images/7a/7a23cbece856b7b842d5907665af5ea593a06faea79283b1be13fc4382e0bf26.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(-2,1)$ and $Q(-2,3)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](images/82/82c921570bbc1ce700db5472871048c14c67df7d6895962f87454c70fc1ce192.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of $P(-2,1)$ satisfy $y=x+3.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $∂A,$ the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The coordinates of $P(-2,1)$ do not satisfy the inequality $y<x+3.$ Hence, $P$ does not lie in the set $A.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, $Q$ is not an interior point of $A$ since any neighborhood of $Q$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I only.'"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4845966-372c-548d-a64a-8d5c7c19d0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453580} {:answer/id #uuid "f1849a3b-58bc-5f4a-b012-a58f9871612b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4845966-372c-548d-a64a-8d5c7c19d0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453580} :answer-field/id #uuid "d47284cf-891c-5cb8-ba28-4824c46e48a5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37544ac-2fca-57be-8001-9189226db946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453582} {:answer/id #uuid "70351b57-7f19-5fbe-be03-fa7da2c1b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70351b57-7f19-5fbe-be03-fa7da2c1b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453583} :answer-field/id #uuid "69249cbb-7e3c-531b-bd6d-21bc466588de" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "433a72ab-7d38-5e4a-8f83-e3fe8097b4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453584} {:answer/id #uuid "09e2b953-fb38-58ce-a5b6-d43d2e3d4354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "433a72ab-7d38-5e4a-8f83-e3fe8097b4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453584} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58739c5-1889-5e03-9e74-ee19d0f13dfc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10dc60fb-f25e-52f7-9f87-59ad72f93d31" :question/math-academy-id "q-174392" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(c)=0,\\,{1}_{B}(c)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=1$\n- **II.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=0$\n- **III.** $c\\in A\\cap B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c) & =min{{1}_{A}(c),{1}_{B}(c)} \\\\  & =min{0,1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=0,$ we conclude that $c$ does not belong to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbd8a41-022e-505a-9a23-5897ee2615d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453946} {:answer/id #uuid "e964dc82-e823-526c-bb4e-d9d86b715c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbd8a41-022e-505a-9a23-5897ee2615d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453946} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5d2420-05be-505d-a6da-9370564b875a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bfaf3e3-c8c3-5b0f-905a-7cfc3c188946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453948} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7b77cf-0808-52a0-92c8-aef31c85857a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e7b77cf-0808-52a0-92c8-aef31c85857a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453949} :answer-field/id #uuid "b912caf2-b2fa-5b75-b5a5-849cbfd33c40" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "581a4ee7-2ef6-5d6a-8a10-f2e80e510c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453950} {:answer/id #uuid "b85c6ec3-9718-5d84-925f-86b8f81442df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "581a4ee7-2ef6-5d6a-8a10-f2e80e510c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453950} :answer-field/id #uuid "74197001-61cf-522e-acb4-234d12a1ff07" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aafb0544-5c12-5527-bc2a-2417215aad99" :question/math-academy-id "q-73566" :question/problem "Let \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is **not** invertible\n- **II.** The lines $2x-3y=1$ and $2x-2y=2$ intersect at exactly one point\n- **III.** $Ax=0$ has no solution" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)-(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. \n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false since, according to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3ba979-73eb-55d9-98be-53eb63f15310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454018} {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019} :answer-field/id #uuid "51beb1c0-c434-5ffe-be4f-d1af3a966f94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b27c5d69-4610-55e4-befd-bab1f9f21b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454020} {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2f4dc-0220-560a-b969-e0fb63f01a28" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} {:answer/id #uuid "b3eaef39-5ed2-5d0e-8448-e5d92a445686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} :answer-field/id #uuid "447c453c-9c02-53db-ad8b-23d0593303f4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c7ff497-8845-5d34-a5a1-e0b10d7a1e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-79367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n- **II.** $A$ is not  invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "913e0931-a878-5504-b8b6-00f819edf9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453210} {:answer/id #uuid "461ff5c7-f262-59e0-9e6a-5ccd795fb660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "913e0931-a878-5504-b8b6-00f819edf9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453210} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e294ac2-b715-5c6e-b139-8e2b8b489e3a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e10c2846-bfa3-5599-a565-ba95e776088c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453212} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1227a-6d81-5364-a894-22a85a885507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1227a-6d81-5364-a894-22a85a885507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453213} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eca9126-955c-5afe-833c-fc32a0b53bb9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076b77e2-6bf3-5918-86f9-98829053c98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453214} {:answer/id #uuid "d46b15b3-6f74-5c05-b218-76f6180d184c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076b77e2-6bf3-5918-86f9-98829053c98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453214} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab876604-ae7b-5692-8d5d-ac2e83bc51d1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a38d2c4-5da1-58d9-ad2f-9024e96c37be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453216} {:answer/id #uuid "9261a407-a47e-58cf-876d-d1ebb17244ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9261a407-a47e-58cf-876d-d1ebb17244ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5823a91a-8b7b-550d-a8ed-1b40a6c306e7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29e169b1-20c5-5789-9178-14e4b85ea9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-107117" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $S$ containing $2\\times 2$ matrices that are not invertible. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $S$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $S$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $S$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $S$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then\n${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ each contain a row consisting only of zeros, so they are not invertible. However,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis invertible. So, $S$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, if $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix that is not invertible then $det(A)=0$ and therefore for all $\\alpha \\in R$ \n\n$$\ndet(\\alpha A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot det(A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $S$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $S$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9334923c-62ff-50b8-adbe-4ed7ab4703c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453218} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2db7a3-d7e9-5c61-9a1a-c8ccad0f7961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9334923c-62ff-50b8-adbe-4ed7ab4703c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453218} :answer-field/id #uuid "88d3cf2c-c423-5cb2-8b21-674e6c600f8d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60feee08-64c3-56f4-8e1e-0f648e32b79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453220} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e281ee-4ace-5610-abf0-889d1b9c58f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60feee08-64c3-56f4-8e1e-0f648e32b79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453220} :answer-field/id #uuid "d281628a-7f5d-5b5e-8c75-4073b51e06b7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "293add60-7966-5c7b-bdde-bcdfd26149d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453222} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf78bf8-3d10-5489-99dd-ef227e9a7758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "293add60-7966-5c7b-bdde-bcdfd26149d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453222} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00a0fe6-f9a7-5605-ad3a-48fa5eb0728e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebc8a07b-3466-5170-9f69-0e8c3685f3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453224} {:answer/id #uuid "1f40564c-9555-5959-bca0-0f63995ff413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f40564c-9555-5959-bca0-0f63995ff413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453225} :answer-field/id #uuid "affc55ed-ee15-5b9d-b758-210c15c8f69b" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff663474-9982-50d0-b983-22c1b4e4d38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107144" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[0,1]\\,|\\,\\,f(x)\\le 1\\,\\,∀x\\in [0,1]}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $B$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if  $f(x)=g(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(x) & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1].$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. Let, for example,  $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ and take and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(x) & =2f(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1].$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9c8b6f7-a765-51f0-bdc1-0e20609fa1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453226} {:answer/id #uuid "75058ef8-65b5-5339-9bcb-1c1175a9c585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9c8b6f7-a765-51f0-bdc1-0e20609fa1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453226} :answer-field/id #uuid "603a8296-6812-5aa0-acca-2e58013b4290" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aea5044e-ffdb-5981-9a0d-1e77af7bb0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453228} {:answer/id #uuid "5e12f28f-5d7e-5ae4-9e88-d666b37d25f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea5044e-ffdb-5981-9a0d-1e77af7bb0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453228} :answer-field/id #uuid "2086fc9f-b317-5fdc-9df7-fec846619a6b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73efe5e7-86d9-56bf-883f-fdf28547d599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453230} {:answer/id #uuid "a85494a0-51a8-59e6-96b9-be4532a22c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73efe5e7-86d9-56bf-883f-fdf28547d599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453230} :answer-field/id #uuid "a819ffc8-0ac7-5428-aa18-b902a7881f2c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94acce7b-7200-5224-a551-0f52dea34c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453232} {:answer/id #uuid "5cef8fe4-d2dc-5067-8776-abd7c9ca57d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cef8fe4-d2dc-5067-8776-abd7c9ca57d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453233} :answer-field/id #uuid "88425d2a-b4ad-54eb-89a3-3a3b986d9505" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ecd1a414-f091-5cfd-86f0-d0c82f6d9564" :question/math-academy-id "q-107147" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $K$ containing all nonconstant functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $K$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $K$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $K$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is a constant function if $f(x)=\\text{constant}$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, the functions $f(x)=x+2$ and $f(x)=-x-1$ are in $K$, however\n\n$$\n(f+g)(x)=1\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1]$ and hence $f+g$ is a constant function. \nSo, $K$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, the product of the scalar zero by any function is the constant function zero. So, $K$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $K$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9adda67-6a0c-5ed4-88d6-f2c76756703b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453478} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2f32a5-a444-594a-bc7b-ca880ea1cd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2f32a5-a444-594a-bc7b-ca880ea1cd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453479} :answer-field/id #uuid "15835f11-1852-5f58-8f9c-38beabfab106" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9fc8eb5-59a6-579e-81ba-64fd489210be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453480} {:answer/id #uuid "af6822f2-5255-5beb-841a-3c878f5590b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9fc8eb5-59a6-579e-81ba-64fd489210be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453480} :answer-field/id #uuid "22ca5593-aa89-50a4-ac84-0aa89a5388d2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75722349-8129-514e-85ed-4febc75783fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453482} {:answer/id #uuid "670ceb03-fec6-5ece-97e4-9b966c32f487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "670ceb03-fec6-5ece-97e4-9b966c32f487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453483} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a80115-d74f-5e30-affe-dd0cd38775ee" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cfd8147-c3e0-5cab-9b14-cee4034ac307" :question/math-academy-id "q-161623" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- **II.** $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\n- **III.** $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "103ba745-89da-572a-8645-0e48e298eb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453628} {:answer/id #uuid "6db316e3-11cf-581e-aba4-72198d752449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103ba745-89da-572a-8645-0e48e298eb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453628} :answer-field/id #uuid "08fbb3c2-9e09-5166-81cf-b13e5f40f715" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454564} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8908055-e767-5cc9-8603-c9755f6acf08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453630} {:answer/id #uuid "2dee54e9-a7cf-5ff7-8cb7-66dd7d69200c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8908055-e767-5cc9-8603-c9755f6acf08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453630} :answer-field/id #uuid "605e62e8-9662-50d1-bfd8-1829ceb621ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7adbcc1-3421-5d01-aa06-a9b6e0ef1051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453632} {:answer/id #uuid "502be7d4-5665-556d-b837-f469b7e58366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502be7d4-5665-556d-b837-f469b7e58366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453633} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3efa2ca-31f9-5aba-80a2-9f4d61b15725" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9dc8cb9-65d8-59f4-a25c-a9f9b514997d" :question/math-academy-id "q-182505" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $¬P⇒Q≡P∨¬Q$\n- **II.** $¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧Q$\n- **III.** $¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧¬Q$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $¬P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬(¬P)∨Q,$ which in turn is equivalent to $P∨Q.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. From part I, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬P⇒Q≡P∨Q\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬(P∨Q).\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(¬P⇒Q)$ is equivalent to $¬P∧¬Q.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87ce1ae9-57eb-59cd-8da4-c1a0d3076afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453952} {:answer/id #uuid "ebff1072-dded-550a-b750-8d400dcf93f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ce1ae9-57eb-59cd-8da4-c1a0d3076afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453952} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e09413b-af06-58f6-88c6-125426ab31d4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "776c0c2e-2277-507d-b18d-ed1e84b4ed82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453954} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3dfc88-d38f-581f-9c20-80e64cbb04cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b3dfc88-d38f-581f-9c20-80e64cbb04cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453955} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ee9fb1-8544-5a36-b32c-707df9287960" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36ca50ed-9faf-5c4a-bf22-4d644e34ef62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453956} {:answer/id #uuid "161c0d73-cc78-5569-9199-8fc986254f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36ca50ed-9faf-5c4a-bf22-4d644e34ef62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453956} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b63f72f-ca55-514b-bc37-6bef9f319ce0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb1f3bd1-4155-5e86-902f-cd91483f7d31" :question/math-academy-id "q-74963" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$\n\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $1$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n\n- **III.** The limit exists and is equal to $1$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+(x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{({x}^{2})}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb97b679-ed73-5d50-b8f3-ebd938a5c69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454138} {:answer/id #uuid "e3090b39-70db-561b-9774-7f4d38196900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3090b39-70db-561b-9774-7f4d38196900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454139} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e1f700-4e27-590e-9aea-505c9d96d52c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b77c043e-6368-5cf0-87ba-b422015be2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454140} {:answer/id #uuid "b7139452-025b-5bbb-8b6c-fac373d52ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7139452-025b-5bbb-8b6c-fac373d52ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454141} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b0eb3f5-b781-5609-babf-762a182d38c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530ae441-da27-537e-a55c-72a1a7eaffa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454142} {:answer/id #uuid "42ec41b7-fdfa-5e73-8caa-ca0e1481cad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ec41b7-fdfa-5e73-8caa-ca0e1481cad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454143} :answer-field/id #uuid "f69bf366-d3cc-56cd-81b4-3fe0b32a22ef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53896f78-ec62-5396-8624-7b1c6badc360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454144} {:answer/id #uuid "74d6078b-e09a-5835-921b-48b69ffd8255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53896f78-ec62-5396-8624-7b1c6badc360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454144} :answer-field/id #uuid "57276cd0-38fc-5c29-abd0-eff90122f7d4" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e8696fa-a30e-5b2e-a6f9-20152471933a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94621" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $H$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $H$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0+0=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a matrix such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0\\cdot k=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $H$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f077c77-0570-536a-a8a6-0a63cf4d87ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454146} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1ea41f-315c-59a7-b182-4abf0e4b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef1ea41f-315c-59a7-b182-4abf0e4b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454147} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b59da7-192e-5638-a6d9-30b5ec427b19" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9224e5e7-ecbe-5a8e-8ff9-aa2feb99653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454148} {:answer/id #uuid "3146b088-175e-5e2a-8f28-d752332c1825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9224e5e7-ecbe-5a8e-8ff9-aa2feb99653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454148} :answer-field/id #uuid "a160776e-c9a6-54ab-ba04-03293503bfa9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af3f92e-2bb3-5d0b-b1d2-d97e3317a680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454150} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6f3468-8a4e-525c-91f1-9eb0300f4e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af3f92e-2bb3-5d0b-b1d2-d97e3317a680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454150} :answer-field/id #uuid "de85e3af-f485-549e-af6a-03e3f37ec071" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437f3bf2-f29e-5af5-aed6-837e31083c5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454152} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8c9d8-9e82-5680-a3c9-bb84c07c77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8c9d8-9e82-5680-a3c9-bb84c07c77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454153} :answer-field/id #uuid "82587102-0923-537e-9e88-86ad077d77a6" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02488e4e-8845-5c5e-a156-a562e8b67a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-94627" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $D={[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a<0}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $D$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $D$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $D,$ then  ${a}_{1}<0$ and ${a}_{2}<0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n is a matrix from $D,$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}<0.$ So, $D$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example,  if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $k=-1,$ then $A$ is an element of $D$ and $k\\in R,$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis *not* in  $D.$ So, $D$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $D$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c34e7d59-6bb4-5c2f-808f-212503d55338" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b62692e4-70a9-5b64-b572-8e95101f299d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454262} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f96054-430f-5abb-9738-492912b4513f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f96054-430f-5abb-9738-492912b4513f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454263} :answer-field/id #uuid "52fb6fd8-12c2-5a40-95db-e8d434005870" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43234e8f-f0ca-5794-8734-537c4540ced4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454264} {:answer/id #uuid "aea27afc-4d53-57d1-a1a6-faf52d441711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea27afc-4d53-57d1-a1a6-faf52d441711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454265} :answer-field/id #uuid "f38bf0d7-cb37-587a-8201-a3fd186776a4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f198704-9c2b-52ba-ab29-315f0f4f7390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454266} {:answer/id #uuid "356b12b2-b30c-58ef-898f-2e04dbb2332f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "356b12b2-b30c-58ef-898f-2e04dbb2332f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454267} :answer-field/id #uuid "d51aab6a-c250-5230-a3e0-85d81f4fb26b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cf92ef9-ce4a-5cbb-9e9d-9e8a2989e53d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97944" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\lambda =-2$ is an eigenvalue of $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(B+2I)x=0$ has a nonzero solution\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $3\\times 3$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=3=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=B+2I.$\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that if $\\lambda =-2$ is an eigenvalue of $B,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(B+2I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, the matrix $M=B+2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Since $M=B+2I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c34e7d59-6bb4-5c2f-808f-212503d55338" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a8febcf-d8f8-5bb1-bd0f-5ea5157901db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454268} {:answer/id #uuid "0d0ab0d9-c27a-5f5c-af64-9667450caa58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a8febcf-d8f8-5bb1-bd0f-5ea5157901db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454268} :answer-field/id #uuid "8384c379-0806-5ddf-b3d0-e3b82670fa9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26764f15-21bd-5865-b436-a36b9b696003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454270} {:answer/id #uuid "a796bded-1ab7-53dd-8b24-5a4f06d7d263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a796bded-1ab7-53dd-8b24-5a4f06d7d263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454271} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6693f4-1188-5c06-b9f9-4c671b8a0599" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f7d45de-1453-5098-a4a6-edffb970d0d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454272} {:answer/id #uuid "89362b6b-2fd1-52b4-a6a5-5b6f4d773b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89362b6b-2fd1-52b4-a6a5-5b6f4d773b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454273} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ba61e62-3f3b-5078-93dc-7f400ec2f0c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f636785f-61ec-504d-b842-394a5a79199b" :question/math-academy-id "q-97947" :question/problem "If $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(C-2I)x=0$ has only zero solution\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{4}$\n- **III.** $\\text{Null}(C-2I)\\ne {0}$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=C-2I.$\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that if $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(C-2I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $C.$ As a result, the matrix $M=C-2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Since $M=C-2I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{4},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(C-2I)\\ne {0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f28abe1-7ce7-5fcd-800c-5355d28b4dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454274} {:answer/id #uuid "975b6d1f-67e4-5ad0-a60c-f212c150bba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975b6d1f-67e4-5ad0-a60c-f212c150bba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454275} :answer-field/id #uuid "01e4ad4b-797b-5e1c-957c-e3b4e3622e5b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b268ef17-aa66-5222-b880-47a780072089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454276} {:answer/id #uuid "98e68f38-5fa0-5696-a788-a965baf32116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b268ef17-aa66-5222-b880-47a780072089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454276} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec0d8911-05a3-5867-85d8-d03e8d8a263a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9e6411f-f645-554b-849c-9e1f5f16f32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454278} {:answer/id #uuid "0df6ff7c-41ab-51b6-a2ff-1f6813596ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df6ff7c-41ab-51b6-a2ff-1f6813596ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8031e5cb-78c7-579e-9e68-cf112703c2a4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a33206bb-7969-5524-a745-290fffeff16f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97967" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(B-2I)=3,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)=1$\n- **II.** $B-2I$ is non-singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $4$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(B-2I) & =4-\\text{rank}(B-2I) \\\\  & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements II is false. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $B-2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that if $M=B-2I$ is singular, then $(B-2I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6d9971d-5d83-5fb4-86e2-96890c06d6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453138} {:answer/id #uuid "c4baccc4-826f-558c-ba91-c27ae92daa70" :answer/type 