swer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32986725-0ef3-5392-8fb4-f9776573a8e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-104963" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-1)^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n- **III.** $f$ is **onto**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function. \n\n![](images/80/80630fae7c4f1e29d855e9a68917156ccf3ecbefd0efc7bda5a9bd0e903c90db.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph covers all $y$-values, so the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, $f$ is a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1324fd0b-5388-5133-ad6a-72d658e3c903" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98b76f87-f94e-56d3-ba42-0328d0629905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453144} {:answer/id #uuid "cac97186-8fdb-55cb-97bb-93817d0b76d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac97186-8fdb-55cb-97bb-93817d0b76d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453145} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5a94acd-57f3-5a96-9735-1e41ec135083" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95822514-1fc2-59c2-94d4-3687e2703a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453146} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec5885f-15fd-5f98-81d7-5c15f34d9ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95822514-1fc2-59c2-94d4-3687e2703a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453146} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2fea8c-4b25-504f-a06f-56c15f1d78b4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "647883ae-2527-55aa-bf65-dcb7dbc6f247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453148} {:answer/id #uuid "c93a1492-d654-57e4-a685-06b45f628115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "647883ae-2527-55aa-bf65-dcb7dbc6f247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453148} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d5c78f3-11e4-5d65-b68c-c2307aee7001" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18cf57da-d5c7-5b11-9220-be1574e018d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104983" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to [-2,2]$ which is given by $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[0,2]$\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in [-2,2],$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n- **III.** $f$ is **onto**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/e1/e1a02621cfacc791c1b100b01957195f1f41e9bf78b65286eabbd13363930c67.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$  in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $2$ and the lowest $y$-value is $0.$ The graph covers all $y$-values between $0$ and $2$, including these numbers, so the range of the function is $[0,2].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Consider, for example,  $y=-1.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $[-2,2],$ there exists some $x$ contained in $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $[-2,2].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48355326-ad4b-578d-906e-404260be62dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453288} {:answer/id #uuid "137c30dc-eac8-5144-aa6e-ecac88c88768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "137c30dc-eac8-5144-aa6e-ecac88c88768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453289} :answer-field/id #uuid "029df452-27e1-55c2-95cc-c51c4094c660" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79a7166-446d-5b5a-a95f-e732499d72f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453290} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2b1e1d-e940-5f7a-a610-b38db6adeb6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c79a7166-446d-5b5a-a95f-e732499d72f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453290} :answer-field/id #uuid "e492fc36-ff9b-5ce9-b63f-47f732639a39" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f22ea7c-9234-582e-9fd8-6c4d53049067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453292} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae5ae4c-d9b5-5c1e-8df4-fc71fc9b7598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ae5ae4c-d9b5-5c1e-8df4-fc71fc9b7598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453293} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f48fb4-a9ca-5657-b58f-f9b05523a3e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d9c3015-ea78-542d-9de3-a1c266f8369d" :question/math-academy-id "q-111793" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨1,1⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, The condition $\\text{rank}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, $T$ is surjective and so  $⟨1,1⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T).$\n\n- Statement II is false. The condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d96ac2-a71a-5eae-a1f2-a35c4f4a3421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453374} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf2f7f5-879e-5b50-99b0-b4a8aef4ece7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d96ac2-a71a-5eae-a1f2-a35c4f4a3421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453374} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa0701da-b463-5213-94f2-e02a73ff00ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aed5c28-8075-55ae-90c0-2b3580818ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453376} {:answer/id #uuid "9429cccf-885a-5592-a530-ce21f4be12af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aed5c28-8075-55ae-90c0-2b3580818ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453376} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a8eabc0-30ea-5a23-bb5c-bfb9f407a0da" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454438} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "594cbcc6-1f78-5c78-a783-2e90c24ef8b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453378} {:answer/id #uuid "7abba252-c5b0-5346-96fe-05d40dee8d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7abba252-c5b0-5346-96fe-05d40dee8d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453379} :answer-field/id #uuid "923ab783-cb50-5906-95f1-23560f2f0e2b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25283dae-901a-5291-a7bb-9324644a9dab" :question/math-academy-id "q-132732" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y}{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The partial derivative with respect to $x$ is defined at $(0,1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n\n- **II.** ${f}_{y}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1,0)$ is defined\n\n- **III.** ${f}_{z}(1,1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{{sin}^{2}⁡z}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{x{sin}^{2}⁡z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is false. If we substitute $(0,1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(0,1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{1}{0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero. Since the function is not defined at the point, the derivative is also undefined.\n\n- Statement II is false. If we substitute $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1,0)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1,0)=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡0}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero. Since the function is not defined at the point, the derivative is also undefined.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{1}{(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{z}$ is also defined at $(1,1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(1,1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-\\frac{(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{(1){sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'III only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdcfad6c-8f67-57f0-8e1a-a5145e94e79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453424} {:answer/id #uuid "55aeaac9-a576-5295-97bc-ebd0c9e7e4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55aeaac9-a576-5295-97bc-ebd0c9e7e4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453425} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9ba92f-81fd-578e-97ef-9822e2732b3c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fb0a31-52f6-57f8-8ea5-865c224e4380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453426} {:answer/id #uuid "6acfaf3d-0245-5aea-b43a-808e8113c3a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22fb0a31-52f6-57f8-8ea5-865c224e4380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453426} :answer-field/id #uuid "79204f72-f15b-57b1-8a43-ec32e3cd9f9d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e76b6fa9-4472-508a-aa11-4fb247f3829f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453428} {:answer/id #uuid "10a94ed2-5542-5c9a-944e-4e6ce2994230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10a94ed2-5542-5c9a-944e-4e6ce2994230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453429} :answer-field/id #uuid "05f6d47f-184b-59c7-bb64-4405edcb8db2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1896da03-9822-50e1-8935-797efb12d1b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-157255" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =-3[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement I is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50c678ac-6856-5dc5-9afe-44b6fb6311de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453538} {:answer/id #uuid "ad824d0a-7f08-5933-8b16-8402f4a9fd2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad824d0a-7f08-5933-8b16-8402f4a9fd2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453539} :answer-field/id #uuid "56d2618d-d2f9-5b8b-b843-2e6f5786a8b9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae85886-4535-502f-84c0-5a86c1c9c7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453540} {:answer/id #uuid "d9363502-c0da-51ae-a073-e57ff08e4ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ae85886-4535-502f-84c0-5a86c1c9c7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453540} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52ed245-0c82-56d3-b8b0-0c0c07c09cac" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454520} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62b9178a-5f22-57aa-961e-121d6f20d793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453542} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ca2d3b-efcd-5ca0-a83f-3513832fdc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62b9178a-5f22-57aa-961e-121d6f20d793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453542} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a99e775-0837-5864-8cc7-c3563a0e99c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97231f8f-64e5-5ea2-a413-41a730985778" :question/math-academy-id "q-170659" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=(x+1)^{2}-2?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[-2,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n- **III.** $f$ is **onto**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/9e/9e8457a8caa2f9dbdb627521e23029325f9edda757336a7a5fbbffbda14b4985.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$  in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the lowest $y$-value is $-2,$ and it occurs at the point $(-1,-2).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values from $y=-2$ and greater, including the number $-2,$ so the range of the function is $[-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false. Consider $y=-3.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=-3.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9929c09c-8f33-57ee-88cb-38daa710dcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453544} {:answer/id #uuid "1f16da6c-f534-5d72-880c-f328ccd0c191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f16da6c-f534-5d72-880c-f328ccd0c191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453545} :answer-field/id #uuid "9154c3d8-007c-5ee3-8a3b-e0dd67cef6cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8124e520-c402-5a54-9af8-c0ce7d475102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453546} {:answer/id #uuid "bce7b7f6-753e-5b37-b888-86bfae6f9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bce7b7f6-753e-5b37-b888-86bfae6f9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453547} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c84fe16-6e6b-5a98-b741-ab03c807812b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454523} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1a128bf-59d0-5ed3-9481-22081c32fcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453548} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fa2398-f7d9-5cc4-b8aa-f1a48a45fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1fa2398-f7d9-5cc4-b8aa-f1a48a45fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453549} :answer-field/id #uuid "f34b228d-dfef-5a02-826b-d0dc59fab7b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5934422-10d9-59ea-acc1-a33dbe6bcea0" :question/math-academy-id "q-171906" :question/problem "Let $m\\in N$ and $n\\in N.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∃\\,n\\in N,\\,5\\le n.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)$ is $N.$\n- **III.** $∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For every natural $m$ there exists natural $n$ such that $m\\le n.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true since $5\\le n$ for some natural number $n$ (e.g., for $n=6$).\n\n- Statement II is true. The predicate\n\n$$\nP(m):\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\n$$\n\nis true for any natural $m.$ For example,\n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\n$$\n\nis true since we can take $n=2.$ Similarly,\n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,2\\le n\n$$\n\nis true since we can take $n=3.$ And so on. In general, it's sufficient to take $n=m+1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀\\,m\\in N\\,(\\,{{∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n}_{⏟}}_{P(m)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(m)$ is true over the universal set $N.$ And, according to statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5b8712-0349-5ec9-be84-86313e9383f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453664} {:answer/id #uuid "99222c1c-3a4e-584c-88d0-dc8348b68220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f5b8712-0349-5ec9-be84-86313e9383f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453664} :answer-field/id #uuid "68de867c-02cd-57fa-bd09-3c999d6ea9c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311c0395-78e4-5af6-9ae4-5e9d6edf2fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453666} {:answer/id #uuid "532515bd-87e1-5e9b-b032-e51385cc6bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "532515bd-87e1-5e9b-b032-e51385cc6bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453667} :answer-field/id #uuid "5da7d4ee-3b45-5d05-bbd5-5970db34cb14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35033423-0e24-5eb3-ad49-542e49a2f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453668} {:answer/id #uuid "94aaeb7f-f626-58e9-8908-cbdc37a51c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35033423-0e24-5eb3-ad49-542e49a2f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453668} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e46de2-a550-5250-aeda-06a46b9a6b77" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42d7175e-7275-5d58-9cbb-adf651178f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183597" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Z$ and $y\\in Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x+1=0.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)$ is $∅.$\n- **III.** $∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a integer $y$ such that, for every integer $x,$ we have $x+y=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $x+1=0$ is not true for some integer $x.$ Say, for $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The predicate\n\n$$\nP(y):\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\n$$\n\nis false for every value of $y.$ For example,\n\n$$\nP(0):∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x=0\n$$\n\nis false for any $x\\ne 0.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $x\\ne -y$ for any $y\\in Z.$ Therefore, its truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement III is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,y\\in Z\\,(\\,{{∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0}_{⏟}}_{P(y)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(y)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement II, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5b5e933-63cd-5870-9ff5-3e6516c2f0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453782} {:answer/id #uuid "2aef0dc4-b15d-5cd2-a2c5-b65739ff18c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5b5e933-63cd-5870-9ff5-3e6516c2f0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453782} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c056c8-efa4-563a-832c-a22f72e55793" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454641} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d20c045d-a7b6-582a-996a-61a2e3b07ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453784} {:answer/id #uuid "8446b446-cf09-5f50-822c-c972a0839ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d20c045d-a7b6-582a-996a-61a2e3b07ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453784} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9caea3-9b43-5d58-88a6-7f613d2c07c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8d1138-120f-514c-9737-44ab8207b868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453786} {:answer/id #uuid "1497c774-e9e5-56fc-a33f-16e7810e0f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1497c774-e9e5-56fc-a33f-16e7810e0f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453787} :answer-field/id #uuid "79528333-5062-5700-b901-57ac2078cec1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac3fd956-3cf4-5e15-bb4c-d8f2d84edef6" :question/math-academy-id "q-216493" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x<1$ and $|x|\\ge 1.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $R,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n- **II.** The truth set of $P(x)$ is $R.$\n- **III.** $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$x<1$\" is $(-\\infty ,1),$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"$|x|\\ge 1$\" is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,1)\\cap ((-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ))=(-\\infty ,-1].\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne R.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is not empty, the statement $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35db3c9b-02b9-5c7d-a8c1-09176c032e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453934} {:answer/id #uuid "29ce6cf9-27c1-5fd1-8cbf-f6799920b1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ce6cf9-27c1-5fd1-8cbf-f6799920b1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453935} :answer-field/id #uuid "7acd2660-cd2a-577c-9376-da725e19aef5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454717} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad87f6c0-0c68-522a-8122-d035dbe64fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453936} {:answer/id #uuid "859d9311-70b2-5685-b197-4a91254e744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "859d9311-70b2-5685-b197-4a91254e744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453937} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d1d4321-6803-5056-a842-c68247cc1177" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2fda6f3-3bce-51e5-9059-f8105ac02f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453938} {:answer/id #uuid "403cb9a2-360b-5e77-afe9-99e083474952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2fda6f3-3bce-51e5-9059-f8105ac02f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453938} :answer-field/id #uuid "65daae6a-989b-50a5-b441-759088075f44" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa8a43bb-df08-5eee-88ea-f9abcdd2fb8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72011" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}_{y}(1,-1)$ is defined\n\n- **II.** Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,0)$\n\n- **III.** ${f}_{x}(1,1)$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}\\cdot \\frac{-1}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}}{2\\sqrt{x-y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,-1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}={e}^{\\sqrt{2}},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,-1)=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{2}}}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,0)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,0)={e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}={e}^{1}=e,\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,0) & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}}{2\\sqrt{1-0}}=\\frac{{e}^{1}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{e}{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,0) & =-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}}{2\\sqrt{1-0}}=-\\frac{{e}^{1}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=-\\frac{e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(1,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(1,1)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-1}}}{2\\sqrt{1-1}}=\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{0}}=\\frac{1}{0}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and II  only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d1ed56-bfc6-5bda-a5c6-d5385ab5bd77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453940} {:answer/id #uuid "bf41f840-b49c-5384-a274-dfe536fcb33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf41f840-b49c-5384-a274-dfe536fcb33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453941} :answer-field/id #uuid "edafd0ac-42e0-5d4a-be7b-7aa902ffa1b6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060c118c-98d6-5841-94fb-d05d803c937b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453942} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca503bc-9f0b-57b9-9107-116d82172e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "060c118c-98d6-5841-94fb-d05d803c937b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453942} :answer-field/id #uuid "97a453da-0bfb-5722-95ac-96c9ea20e34e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8b8bc4-d09b-5051-b032-eb64e490a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453944} {:answer/id #uuid "5922a222-d689-5f69-94af-6d12b904bec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8b8bc4-d09b-5051-b032-eb64e490a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453944} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e81b99c-60a0-5dd3-8161-a53cd384fae9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff98942c-b72f-558c-86fd-786f6575a16d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72019" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2x+y-z}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}_{y}(1,1,1)$ is defined\n\n- **II.** ${f}_{z}(0,1,2)$ is defined\n\n- **III.** The partial derivative with respect to $x$ is defined at $(0,1,1)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+y-z}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,1,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,1,1)=\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+1-1}=\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,1,1) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+1-1}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. If we substitute $(0,1,2)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(0,1,2)=\\sqrt{2\\cdot 0+1-2}=\\sqrt{-1},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since the number under the radical is negative.\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(0,1,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(0,1,1)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 0+1-1}}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b64c7222-8178-5745-8e74-7d3d3ada236d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454024} {:answer/id #uuid "e561b55b-0014-50e9-9583-fa8316227227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b64c7222-8178-5745-8e74-7d3d3ada236d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454024} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdf7c354-9699-5c96-81a6-477592bd5789" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2af1a7-3c28-56d8-928f-ef61266cf553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454026} {:answer/id #uuid "2eed2737-812f-5961-9396-c460b64bbd69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2eed2737-812f-5961-9396-c460b64bbd69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454027} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f44b5c3-35bf-51b2-aaca-38d7b8b70d4f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf8d5f67-d6d3-51d6-ad2b-8ee69006b10c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454028} {:answer/id #uuid "fc265a77-f3c2-54a8-bb4c-ef3c2eef3d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc265a77-f3c2-54a8-bb4c-ef3c2eef3d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454029} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b10f796-218a-5bcd-aac9-a709584f5702" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9c388c8-17e9-5b67-9968-fd45f98197a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-80261" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={x}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n- **III.** $f$ is **onto**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function. \n\n![](images/1a/1a2b29a675770d1c8331672656a6054b052ebfebdf6bc61e5bd6459468087215.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph covers all $y$-values, so the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, $f$ is a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1324fd0b-5388-5133-ad6a-72d658e3c903" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947844cd-1269-59a2-9579-38c3bf5a1be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454030} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b66751-c728-5194-852e-fce7cee82cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b66751-c728-5194-852e-fce7cee82cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454031} :answer-field/id #uuid "eee835c5-8b1e-58cf-86a7-d01172af5440" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454765} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2add6c0f-1b98-5085-885c-4f5943c964ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454032} {:answer/id #uuid "5aeaced6-0274-5f64-9e42-e938b5c58ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2add6c0f-1b98-5085-885c-4f5943c964ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454032} :answer-field/id #uuid "88a19825-3e91-5892-ac06-9e5a82fc51df" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66953d10-bfc0-555b-8107-3a6726174100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454034} {:answer/id #uuid "b957c21c-274f-5957-b83e-f42201b11e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66953d10-bfc0-555b-8107-3a6726174100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454034} :answer-field/id #uuid "b28a6f71-cba3-51e4-bc5d-72a067179d3e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5848bc45-4fef-5470-b7b2-022f9067ecb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80297" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[0,3]\\to [0,8]$ which is given by $y={2}^{x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[1,8]$\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in [0,8],$ $∃\\,x\\in [0,3]$ such that $f(x)=y$\n- **III.** $f$ is **onto**" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/47/47407d426cf9bb816c0b3dd052138b637bc73e7aa6d751278b20d8add020526d.png)\n\n \nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $8$ and the lowest $y$-value is $1.$ The graph covers all $y$-values between $1$ and $8$, including these numbers, so the range of the function is indeed $[1,8].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Consider, for example,  $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x\\in [0,3]$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $[0,8],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $[0,3]$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $[0,3]$ onto $[0,8].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6a14e7a-b747-5daa-a6d8-ddf27bcb3435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454054} {:answer/id #uuid "ef203a18-6200-50a4-8f37-40f6d775a047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6a14e7a-b747-5daa-a6d8-ddf27bcb3435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454054} :answer-field/id #uuid "368e434e-c352-5632-8222-8c74717eb1e3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89d2bcf1-e624-5732-9da9-f26392281661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454056} {:answer/id #uuid "65454c69-ffda-5315-a369-0369fd32aa73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65454c69-ffda-5315-a369-0369fd32aa73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454057} :answer-field/id #uuid "1998fa1f-9db2-528c-8a77-26d7fb35e77f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a0139cb-9ef6-5b37-92da-cfe05b47fe33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454058} {:answer/id #uuid "03dcd1c2-23f1-50a4-923d-5b396bf94b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03dcd1c2-23f1-50a4-923d-5b396bf94b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454059} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fd599f9-74b2-5a43-9569-f24f6afb0be6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47830ab2-2bae-52c6-8c9c-df89a69a6369" :question/math-academy-id "q-80536" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{R}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,2]$\n\n- **II.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/5c/5c5dbc673c2c6a9bd0a4f06223133e21e2dcbbdbaa2dfe2de2b29d8824dd821e.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$ Also, the integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statements II and III are true. In both cases, the rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d21b03-b4aa-5edf-97d9-e8d82ba76aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454250} {:answer/id #uuid "a4df005b-76b4-5349-9381-8a02c4118a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48d21b03-b4aa-5edf-97d9-e8d82ba76aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454250} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0c8fb9-1191-5fbe-89aa-082fed4cfe5c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46db31c3-b479-5b1f-9f99-dea7a4e5f9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454252} {:answer/id #uuid "6adfd406-7a7b-520c-b675-6259bd0b2894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46db31c3-b479-5b1f-9f99-dea7a4e5f9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454252} :answer-field/id #uuid "61692f77-337b-53e8-9104-052d1bee29b9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bf8b14e-2ea8-5937-a61f-4fbf1ad7451e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454254} {:answer/id #uuid "3f5d6c2c-7493-5064-bdb2-fd8b5146ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f5d6c2c-7493-5064-bdb2-fd8b5146ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454255} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfa9f97-b5ce-506a-a8e7-d728d9426d04" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5aa9ee11-e88d-5123-8f62-331a18227a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97075" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ to the origin. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(T)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is the zero-subspace ${0},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=0\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have that\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666fa542-cf57-5c1b-8235-fd0e152853d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454256} {:answer/id #uuid "011063c3-9666-5b11-8325-d5a53f0ca7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011063c3-9666-5b11-8325-d5a53f0ca7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454257} :answer-field/id #uuid "251c5103-04e9-5f82-9799-dce064a89e0b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859bf573-b364-5fe7-906a-1889b6b49ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454258} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7f0115-a5c9-53d6-a054-0f8b8da7d2d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "859bf573-b364-5fe7-906a-1889b6b49ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454258} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fba21ba-604e-5a02-b4e4-86f7b393c68e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "737fb959-5d8a-5e06-a11d-18a5e40324a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454260} {:answer/id #uuid "afff2fb7-4c9e-5490-b6a1-72764933cd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "737fb959-5d8a-5e06-a11d-18a5e40324a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454260} :answer-field/id #uuid "d766cf66-eb67-509f-bfcf-670ca1d9a88f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f9ccb581-9372-57d1-992f-f285342045f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-97080" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=-2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨-1,2⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=1,\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the point $(-1,2)$ satisfies the equation of the line $y=-2x$ since $2=-2\\cdot (-1).$ Hence, \n\n$$\n⟨-1,2⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(T)=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c915f3d8-89f2-53ed-aef0-20b410b54630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453150} {:answer/id #uuid "3f37584d-1373-5be8-ac5a-8410240fe69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f37584d-1373-5be8-ac5a-8410240fe69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453151} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c663f3-33fc-5e6d-b766-632d1b4cd482" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbf1e044-84c3-5f30-a402-f435bec02e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453152} {:answer/id #uuid "b6dee32f-9add-502d-baa1-906900439c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6dee32f-9add-502d-baa1-906900439c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453153} :answer-field/id #uuid "99235344-66bd-542f-8c3c-ebc972c3c1c0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a477356-2383-5fed-af7d-7bac2355443f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453154} {:answer/id #uuid "6878e6e9-6904-523a-bf6f-59f21f65cbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6878e6e9-6904-523a-bf6f-59f21f65cbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453155} :answer-field/id #uuid "00328259-8f3e-5a30-b032-16741e404afb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b421e9a7-e6c7-514b-9eac-4c4a22d0b15a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105133" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=x+2?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(-1)\\ne f(1)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is an injection" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/3b/3b849edf2ae8976e0abd5e0aa43180ad61d90b01d6f229c2b7fc7898ea860400.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(-1)=(-1)+2=1$ and $f(1)=1+2=3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}]}
